---
// Public account-deletion page for Velko (Google Play's "delete account URL"
// requirement). Keep in step with the deletion section of the Privacy Policy.
import VelkoDoc from '../../layouts/VelkoDoc.astro';
import { velkoOperator } from '../../data/velkoOperator';

const lastUpdated = '14 October 2026';
const email = velkoOperator.email;
const deleteMail = `mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Delete my Velko account')}`;
---

<VelkoDoc
  title="Velko — Delete your account"
  description="How to delete your Velko account and data, what is deleted, and what is kept and for how long."
  heading="Delete your Velko account"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
>
  <p class="doc-lead">
    You can delete your Velko account, and the personal data that goes with it, at any time.
    Velko is the water sports gear rental app operated by {velkoOperator.name}
    (NIPC {velkoOperator.nipc}), {velkoOperator.address}.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li>Open Velko and sign in.</li>
    <li>Go to <strong>Profile</strong>.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Delete account</strong> and confirm.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Deletion happens straight away. If you have a rental in progress, finish or cancel it first.
    Booking requests nobody has answered yet are withdrawn for you.
  </p>

  <h2>By email</h2>
  <p>
    If you can't use the app, email <a href={deleteMail}>{email}</a> from the email address on
    your Velko account, with the subject “Delete my Velko account”. If you signed in with
    Apple and hid your email, write from the Apple ID email and tell us so; we may ask you to
    confirm the request before acting on it. We delete the account within 30 days of receiving
    the request, and confirm by email when it's done.
  </p>

  <h2>What is deleted</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li>Your login, email address, display name and profile photo.</li>
    <li>Your listings, listing photos, pickup addresses and saved gear.</li>
    <li>Your notification tokens, business profile, and your Sign in with Apple authorisation.</li>
    <li>The text of your messages, which is replaced with “Message deleted”.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is kept, and for how long</h2>
  <p>
    Some records have to be kept after your account is gone, either because the law requires it
    or so the other person on a rental keeps their record. Your name on them is replaced with
    “Deleted user”, and each is deleted automatically when its period ends.
  </p>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li><strong>Bookings, payments, fees and invoices</strong>: 10 years, for Portuguese accounting and tax law.</li>
    <li><strong>Seller details already used in a DAC7 tax report</strong> (owners only): 10 years, as tax law requires.</li>
    <li><strong>Handover and claim photos, reviews and claims of past rentals</strong>: 36 months after the rental ends, the period in which a claim about it can usually still be made.</li>
    <li><strong>Reports and moderation records</strong>: 36 months after the report is made.</li>
    <li><strong>Crash and diagnostic reports</strong>: 90 days.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The <a href="/velko/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> has the full details, including how to get
    a copy of your data before you delete your account.
  </p>

  <p class="doc-note">
    Deleting your Velko account doesn't close the Stripe account you may have set up for
    payouts as an owner. Stripe keeps its own records under
    <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</VelkoDoc>
